 10: J=125,K=38 → KEEP\nRow 11: J=189,K=2 → KEEP\nRow 12: J=32,K=140 → KEEP\nRow 13: J=75,K=1 → KEEP\nRow 14: J=1.77,K=81 → KEEP\nRow 15: J=0.75,K=375 → KEEP\nRow 16: J=230,K=1 → KEEP\nRow 17: J=45.45,K=9 → KEEP\nRow 18: J=blank, K=\"-\" → DELETE\nRow 19: J=blank, K=0 → DELETE\nRow 20: J=blank, K=0 → DELETE\nRow 21: J=blank, K=51872.34 → KEEP (K has data)\nRow 22: J=\"-\", K=blank → DELETE (both meet criteria)\nRow 23: J=2.7,K=1534 → KEEP\n...\nRow 29: J=blank, K=blank → DELETE\nRow 52: J=blank,K=59583.03 → KEEP\nRow 53: J=0, K=\"$\" → both meet criteria → DELETE\nRow 54: J=2.7, K=4375 → KEEP\n\nLet me write a script to do this. The headers remain as row 1. I'll keep header row and reorder remaining rows.\n\nLet me write the script.\n\n","input_tokens":4658,"output_tokens":1289,"latency_ms":27088,"error":null,"tool":"bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd /workspace/task && cat > solve.py << 'EOF'\nimport openpyxl\n\npath = \"/workspace/task/output.xlsx\"\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook(path)\nws = wb[\"Sheet2\"]\n\nbad = {\"\", \"-\", \"0\", \"$\", \"$0\", \"$0.0\"}\n\ndef is_bad(v):\n    if v is None:\n        return True  # blank\n    if isinstance(v, str):\n        return v.strip() in bad\n    # numeric\n    return str(v) == \"0\"\n\n# read all rows\nrows = []\nfor r in range(1, ws.max_row+1):\n    vals = [ws.cell(row=r, column=c).value for c in range(1, 12)]\n    rows.append(vals)\n\n# keep header\nnew_rows = [rows[0]]\nfor i, vals in enumerate(rows[1:], start=2):\n    j = vals[9]\n    k = vals[10]\n    if is_bad(j) and is_bad(k):\n        continue  # delete\n    new_rows.append(vals)\n\n# clear old content\nfor r in range(1, ws.max_row+1):\n    for c in range(1, 12):\n        ws.cell(row=r, column=c).value = None\n\n# write new rows\nfor r, vals in enumerate(new_rows, start=1):\n    for c, v in enumerate(vals, start=1):\n        ws.cell(row=r, column=c).value = v\n\nwb.save(path)\nprint(\"kept rows:\", len(new_rows))\nEOF\npython3 solve.py"},"tool_output":{"exitCode":0,"stderr":"","stdout":"kept rows: 45\n","truncated":false}}
